  "result": "I implemented issue #12 and opened a PR: https://github.com/acme/textstats/pull/7. It's on a new branch, `feature/top-words-12`.\n\n- **Change:** `top_words(text, n)` is in `textstats/__init__.py`, stdlib only as the reviewer asked. It returns `(word, count)` tuples, most frequent first and at most `n` of them. Matching ignores case and punctuation, ties go alphabetically, and empty text gives `[]`.\n- **Tests:** I added 9 unit tests to `tests/test_textstats.py`, covering each acceptance criterion plus `n=0` and `n` larger than the vocabulary. The full suite passes: 12 tests OK. I re-ran it myself before committing.\n- **Plan:** I skipped a separate planning step because the change was small and fully specified by the issue.\n\nOne behavior you may want to change: punctuation is deleted, not treated as a word break. So `don't` counts as `dont` and `well-known` as `wellknown`. I noted this in the PR body. If you'd rather split at punctuation, so `don't` becomes `don` and `t`, it's a small change.",
